NNAAMMEE
       mcookie - generate magic cookies for xauth

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       mmccooookkiiee [options]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       mmccooookkiiee generates a 128-bit random hexadecimal number for use with the
       X authority system. Typical usage:

          xxaauutthh aadddd ::00 .. mcookie

       The "random" number generated is actually the MD5 message digest of
       random information coming from one of the sources ggeettrraannddoomm(2) system
       call, _/_d_e_v_/_u_r_a_n_d_o_m, _/_d_e_v_/_r_a_n_d_o_m, or the _l_i_b_c _p_s_e_u_d_o_-_r_a_n_d_o_m _f_u_n_c_t_i_o_n_s,
       in this preference order. See also the option ----ffiillee.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --ff, ----ffiillee _f_i_l_e
           Use this _f_i_l_e as an additional source of randomness (for example
           _/_d_e_v_/_u_r_a_n_d_o_m). When _f_i_l_e is '-', characters are read from standard
           input.

       --mm, ----mmaaxx--ssiizzee _n_u_m_b_e_r
           Read from _f_i_l_e only this _n_u_m_b_e_r of bytes. This option is meant to
           be used when reading additional randomness from a file or device.

           The _n_u_m_b_e_r argument may be followed by the multiplicative suffixes
           KiB=1024, MiB=1024*1024, and so on for GiB, TiB, PiB, EiB, ZiB and
           YiB (the "iB" is optional, e.g., "K" has the same meaning as "KiB")
           or the suffixes KB=1000, MB=1000*1000, and so on for GB, TB, PB,
           EB, ZB and YB.

       --vv, ----vveerrbboossee
           Inform where randomness originated, with amount of entropy read
           from each source.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Print version and exit.

FFIILLEESS
       _/_d_e_v_/_u_r_a_n_d_o_m

       _/_d_e_v_/_r_a_n_d_o_m

BBUUGGSS
       It is assumed that none of the randomness sources will block.

